{"kind":"artifact","text":"Implementation report for landing-obligation I2 (request a374fbf4) at exact head 28ff5c60f732684c9bef388726c1edc101874709 on request/landing-obligation-i2, three commits over main 6bcd22b4, thirteen changed paths, no ui or embed change; supersedes the report 507f97b8 at 18b5d7d2 after planner reproduced that a pre-commit hook could retarget HEAD after the last measurement so the merge commit landed on another branch while the receipt sealed main. The landing no longer commits through HEAD: after preflight the merged index is written with write-tree, the merge commit is created with commit-tree using the sealed pre-head as first parent and the candidate as second (no hooks, no HEAD dependence, message bytes identical to git commit and asserted), and the sealed target ref is advanced by update-ref compare-and-swap against the sealed pre-head; a ref that moved keeps its move and the unreferenced commit is unreachable; the checkout is caught up only while HEAD still names the sealed ref, otherwise the landing stands on the ref and the checkout is reported as no longer standing on it. Planner hook repro ported as TestMergeLandsOnTheSealedRefWhenAHookRetargetsHead (red at 18b5d7d2, green here); TestMergeRefusesWhenTheTargetMovesBeforeTheLanding goes red when the CAS old value is dropped; restoring git commit turns the hook test red. Two documented consequences: commit hooks no longer run for a merge, and --text reaches the receipt verbatim. Everything from 18b5d7d2 stands: merge_target_repo, merge_target_ref and merge_hold_warning sealed durably and as Gitseq-Target-Repo, Gitseq-Target-Ref and Gitseq-Hold-Warning trailers; destination measured from the checkout and compared with the fold-resolved target; refusals for detached, wrong branch, wrong repository and movement between planning and landing; unsolicited --authorization refused on an unheld request; held-without-release lands with a stderr warning and merge_hold_warning=true for the windo